<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - IBM downgraded.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - IBM downgraded.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Merrill Lynch analyst Dan Mandresh has cut his rating for International Business Machines Corp to near-term neutral from near-term buy, a market source said on Friday.</p>
<p>-- Mandresh kept IBM's rating as a long-term buy.</p>
<p>-- In a report, he wrote that earnings would be disappointing in coming quarters, the source said.</p>
<p>-- Mandresh cut his estimate for first quarter earnings per share (EPS) to $2.10 from $2.32 and to $2.60 from $2.90 for the second quarter.</p>
<p>-- Shares in the company closed on Thursday at 131-3/8.</p>
<p>((-- Wall Street desk (212) 859-1730))</p>
</text>
